\ A comparison leaves a Bool, not 0 or 1, so adding it to a count is a type
\ error: `Int` and `Bool` are distinct types and neither is read as the
\ other. The checker must refuse the `prim +`, whose top input is the Bool.
: count-positive
  (forall ρ; ρ n:Int^many x:Int^many -- ρ r:Int^many)
  0 prim > prim + ;
